.TH BZ3GREP 1 "2026-10-20" "bzip3-rs" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bz3grep, bz3egrep, bz3fgrep \- search possibly compressed files for a pattern
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bz3grep
.RI [ grep_options ]
.I pattern
.RI [ files... ]
.br
.B bz3egrep
.RI [ grep_options ]
.I pattern
.RI [ files... ]
.br
.B bz3fgrep
.RI [ grep_options ]
.I pattern
.RI [ files... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bz3grep
searches the plain form of each named file for
.IR pattern .
A file starting with the
.B BZ3v1
magic is decompressed with
.B "bzip3 \-dcfq"
; any other file is read directly.
A bare name
.I foo
also matches
.IR foo.bz3 ,
as with the bzip2 wrapper.
.PP
The program name selects the search tool:
.B bz3egrep
uses
.BR egrep ,
.B bz3fgrep
uses
.BR fgrep ,
and
.B bz3grep
uses
.BR grep
(or the
.BR $GREP ,
.BR $EGREP ,
.BR $FGREP
overrides).
.BR \-e ,
.BR \-f ,
.BR \-A ,
and
.B \-B
are forwarded to the search tool.
With no files, standard input is probed for the magic and searched.
.PP
With several files, each match is prefixed with the file name.
.B \-h
suppresses the prefix;
.B \-l
lists matching file names only.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status is that of the search tool: 0 on match, 1 on no
match, and 2 on error. The status of the last failing file is kept.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bzip3 (1),
.BR grep (1),
.BR bz3diff (1),
.BR bz3more (1)
